Creating a Child Process Using fork().

Explanation:

Function - Purpose
fork() - Creates a new child process.
getpid() - Returns the current process ID.
getppid() - Returns the parent process ID.


Important concepts:

pid_t – Data type used to store process IDs.
fork() – Creates a child process by duplicating the calling process.
pid == 0 – Indicates execution in the child process.
pid > 0 – Indicates execution in the parent process; the value is the child's PID.
pid < 0 – Indicates that process creation failed.
Parent and child execute independently after fork().
